<%# One sidebar navigation link. Render with `layout:` and pass the icon as a block.

    Locals:
      path   - link target
      label  - visible text
      active - true when this is the current page

    aria-current="page" is what conveys "you are here" to assistive tech - the tint and the
    indicator bar alone would violate WCAG 1.4.1.

    Styling comes from NavHelper, shared with the admin nav. 44px minimum height: a nav row is a
    bare tap target, which is where the 44px figure applies - buttons are on the 40px token.

    This used to be wrapped in <label for="mobile-menu-toggle"> to uncheck the hidden checkbox
    that held the mobile drawer open. The drawer controller closes on navigation instead, once,
    rather than through a wrapper on every row. %>
<li>
  <%= link_to path, aria: { current: ("page" if active) }, class: nav_row_class(active: active) do %>
    <span class="<%= nav_indicator_class(active: active) %>" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center" aria-hidden="true"><%= yield %></span>
    <span><%= label %></span>
  <% end %>
</li>
